{
  "id": "T-28",
  "question": "How does the damage of an explosion fall with distance?",
  "bible": "§11",
  "gameVersion": "44.1.4.1",
  "reports": [
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "Ogris, no mods: 0m: 600, 1m: 576, 2m: 549, 3m: 480, 4m: 400, 5m: 335, 6m: 244, 7m: 117, 8m: 64, 9m: no hit"
    },
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "1. I tried to be \"in the middle\" of where it showed the number. 2. I tried to place them to the side (on the circumference of a circle with the radius as distance). 3. All white but I did not test more than once. 4. Normal Ogris. 5. Hit the body, 75 for Penta and 100 for Ogris matches."
    },
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "Ogris: 7.1m, 80% falloff"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A level 200 Runner, paused in the Simulacrum, and no numbers were predicted to Pavel. A reading of 3 m is taken as its middle, 2.5 m. An explosion counts up to the enemy's body, which is about half a metre out from where the distance is taken to. Placed by eye, so the tolerance is about a third of a metre. The wiki's straight line to the edge damage is far off near the rim. Ogris is not in the library yet.",
